{
  "step_1": "The decision reason evaluates whether each lottery contains a sure outcome (i.e., an outcome with 100% probability) and prefers the lottery that has such a sure outcome. In Lottery A, there are two outcomes: -1000 Euros with 50% probability and 0 Euros with 50% probability. Neither outcome is certain, so Lottery A does not have a sure outcome. In Lottery B, the outcome is -500 Euros with 100% probability, which is a sure outcome. Therefore, the decision reason would prefer Lottery B because it is the only one with a sure outcome. The relevant information (presence of a sure outcome) can be clearly derived from the structure of the lotteries.",
