  "step_3": "The decision reason requires identifying which lottery has a sure outcome and preferring that one. The individual correctly identifies that Lottery A has a sure outcome (guaranteed loss) and Lottery B does not. However, instead of preferring the lottery with the sure outcome (as the reason dictates), the individual chooses the one without it (Lottery B), explicitly stating they are accepting the risk. This indicates that while the individual considered the presence of a sure outcome, they did not follow the rule of the decision reason (which would have led to choosing A). Instead, they weighed the sure loss against the probabilistic large loss and opted for risk-taking. Thus, although the information relevant to the reason was considered, the rule of preferring the sure outcome was not followed. The reason was recognized but not used to make the decision.",
  "final_assessment_score": 30
}

